#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:96
#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:36:<autosummary>:1
msgid "Persistent, grid-strided tile scheduler with L2 swizzle and clustering."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:38
msgid "Module Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:44
msgid ""
"State (single-element ``T.alloc_var`` buffers): ``m_idx`` / ``n_idx`` are "
"the current tile coordinates; ``linear_idx`` is the worker's global linear "
"cursor; ``current_iter`` is the 0-based iteration count (how many tiles this "
"worker has advanced past = the \"wave\" index). Each is exposed as a read-"
"only property returning the scalar ``PrimExpr`` (``sched.m_idx``, ``sched."
"current_iter``); only scheduler methods mutate the underlying buffers "
"(``self._m_idx[0] = ...``). ``current_iter`` is the single iteration clock "
"the kernel can read for pipeline/double-buffer state (e.g. ``sched."
"current_iter & 1``), removing the need for a separate ``for w`` loop "
"counter. Subclasses implement ``update_current_idx`` to decode "
"``linear_idx`` into ``(m_idx, n_idx)`` and set ``self._total_tiles`` (used "
"by ``valid``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:59
msgid "Current tile row as a scalar ``PrimExpr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:64
msgid "Current tile column as a scalar ``PrimExpr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:69
msgid "This worker's global linear tile cursor as a scalar ``PrimExpr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:74
msgid "0-based iteration count (wave index) as a scalar ``PrimExpr``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:93
msgid "Bases: :py:obj:`BaseTileScheduler`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:98
msgid ""
"The 2D tile grid (``num_m_tiles`` x ``num_n_tiles``) is flattened into a "
"linear order and distributed across ``num_workers`` persistent workers: "
"worker ``w`` processes linear indices ``w, w + num_workers, ...`` until they "
"run past the total. The linear-to-2D decode is controlled by three "
"independent, interacting factors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:104
msgid ""
"``column_major`` -- traversal order. With ``swizzle_size == 1`` this is pure "
"column-major (``m`` varies fastest) when ``True``, or pure row-major (``n`` "
"varies fastest) when ``False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:107
msgid ""
"``swizzle_size`` -- L2-locality panel width. The \"fast\" axis is widened "
"into panels of ``swizzle_size`` tiles along the \"slow\" axis: a full strip "
"of the fast axis is swept for each group of ``swizzle_size`` slow-axis tiles "
"before advancing. ``swizzle_size == 1`` disables swizzling. This is the "
"CUTLASS-style threadblock swizzle used by the SM100 persistent GEMM "
"examples. Non-divisible tail panels are handled (narrower last panel)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:113
msgid ""
"``cluster_size`` -- block clustering along M (x) only. The M tiles are "
"grouped into clusters of ``cluster_size`` rows, and the scheduler runs at "
"*cluster* granularity: it produces the cluster-row in ``m_idx`` over a grid "
"of ``ceildiv(num_m_tiles, cluster_size)`` cluster-rows x ``num_n_tiles`` "
"columns. The caller turns the cluster-row into a real block row by adding "
"the in-cluster rank::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:120
msgid "bx = sched.m_idx * cluster_size + cta_rank_in_cluster"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:122
msgid "(For ``cluster_size == 1`` this reduces to ``bx = sched.m_idx``.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:124
msgid ""
"Interaction: clustering reshapes the grid to ``M' x N'`` (with ``M' = "
"ceildiv(num_m_tiles, cluster_size)``) *first*; the swizzle and traversal "
"order then operate on that reshaped grid. ``num_workers`` is the number of "
"resident workers (= clusters when ``cluster_size > 1``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:129
msgid "Number of tiles along M (``ceildiv(M, block_M)``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:131
msgid "Number of tiles along N (``ceildiv(N, block_N)``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:133
msgid ""
"Persistent stride = number of resident workers/clusters. Defaults to "
"``driver.get_num_sms() // cluster_size`` (one block per SM, grouped into "
"clusters)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:137
msgid "L2 swizzle panel width (default ``1`` = no swizzle)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:139
msgid "Traversal order (default ``True`` = column-major / M fastest)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:141
msgid "Block-cluster size along M only (default ``1`` = no clustering)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:143
msgid ""
"If ``True`` (default), allocate the ``m_idx`` / ``n_idx`` / ``linear_idx`` / "
"``current_iter`` state buffers and enable ``init`` / ``next_tile`` / "
"``valid`` for a ``while`` persistent loop. If ``False``, allocate no state "
"and expose only the pure ``coord(tile_id) -> (m, n)`` decode (for ``for w in "
"range(waves)`` loops and auto warp-specialization, where the loop owns the "
"iteration clock and the WS pass owns the pipeline phase)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:150
msgid ""
"Optional name prefix for the state buffers in the generated IR (``{name}"
"_m_idx`` / ``{name}_n_idx`` / ...). Default ``None`` leaves the buffers with "
"generic auto-generated names; pass a name to make the IR easier to read when "
"a kernel holds several scheduler instances."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:157
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:158
msgid "Plain persistent GEMM (one block per SM)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:160
msgid ""
"m_blocks, n_blocks = T.ceildiv(M, block_M), T.ceildiv(N, block_N)\n"
"with T.Kernel(driver.get_num_sms(), threads=threads) as (block_id,):\n"
"    sched = T.PersistentTileScheduler(m_blocks, n_blocks)\n"
"    sched.init(block_id)\n"
"    while sched.valid():\n"
"        bx, by = sched.m_idx, sched.n_idx\n"
"        # ... compute tile (bx, by) ...\n"
"        sched.next_tile()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:169
msgid "With L2 swizzle (panel width 8) and named state buffers in the IR::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:171
msgid ""
"sched = T.PersistentTileScheduler(\n"
"    m_blocks, n_blocks, swizzle_size=8, name=\"sched\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:174
msgid "With a 2-CTA cluster along M (e.g. SM100 2-SM MMA)::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:176
msgid ""
"sm_num = driver.get_num_sms()\n"
"cluster_size = 2\n"
"with T.ClusterKernel(sm_num, threads=256, cluster_dims=cluster_size) as "
"(block_id):\n"
"    cta_rank = T.block_rank_in_cluster()\n"
"    sched = T.PersistentTileScheduler(\n"
"        m_blocks, n_blocks,\n"
"        swizzle_size=8, cluster_size=cluster_size)\n"
"    sched.init(block_id // cluster_size)   # init with cluster id\n"
"    while sched.valid():\n"
"        bx = sched.m_idx * cluster_size + cta_rank\n"
"        by = sched.n_idx\n"
"        # ... compute tile (bx, by) ...\n"
"        sched.next_tile()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:190
msgid ""
"Stateless form (``stateful=False``) for ``for w`` loops / auto-WS, where the "
"scheduler is only a tile-coordinate decoder::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:193
msgid ""
"sched = T.PersistentTileScheduler(\n"
"    m_blocks, n_blocks, swizzle_size=8, stateful=False)\n"
"for w in range(waves):\n"
"    bx, by = sched.coord(num_workers * w + worker_id)\n"
"    if bx * block_M < M and by * block_N < N:\n"
"        # ... pipelined inner loop (T.Pipelined / T.copy / T.gemm) ...\n"
"        pass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:201
msgid ""
"Manual warp-specialized kernels use ``current_iter`` as the single iteration "
"clock (no separate ``for w`` loop): each warp role runs its own ``while "
"sched.valid()`` loop and reads ``sched.current_iter`` for pipeline/double-"
"buffer state (``sched.current_iter & 1`` etc.) while reading ``sched."
"m_idx`` / ``sched.n_idx`` for the tile::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:207
msgid ""
"sched.init(block_id)\n"
"while sched.valid():\n"
"    bx, by = sched.m_idx, sched.n_idx\n"
"    # ... use sched.current_iter for barrier phase / double-buffering ...\n"
"    sched.next_tile()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:214
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:215
msgid ""
"State is held in single-element ``T.alloc_var`` buffers behind read-only "
"properties: ``sched.m_idx`` / ``sched.current_iter`` etc. return the scalar "
"``PrimExpr`` directly (no ``[0]``). Only scheduler methods mutate state, via "
"``self._x[0] = ...`` on the underlying buffers; the ``[0]`` is required "
"there for the write to lower to a ``BufferStore``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:239
msgid "Decode a linear ``tile_id`` into ``(m_idx, n_idx)`` (pure PrimExpr)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../autoapi/tilelang/language/tile_schedule/index.rst:241
msgid ""
"Stateless: builds expressions only, touches no state buffer, so it is usable "
"on a ``stateful=False`` instance and can be called independently from any "
"loop / warp role. ``m_idx`` is the cluster row when ``cluster_size > 1`` "
"(caller adds the in-cluster rank)."
msgstr ""
